  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A charming little fishing harbour with its colourful boats, Sanary-sur-Mer has several hotels that accept dogs, handy for exploring this authentic corner between Bandol and Six-Fours-les-Plages. Three confirmed establishments:</p>
      <p><strong>Adonis Sanary — Grand Hôtel des Bains</strong>, 25 boulevard d'Estienne d'Orves: dogs under 10 kg accepted, €10/day supplement plus the tourist tax, notify the hotel in advance (the number of dogs accepted may vary by season). <strong>Hostellerie La Farandole</strong>, 140 chemin de la Plage: a seafront 4-star hotel with a pool, spa and restaurant, dogs accepted with a supplement of around €15/day, size limits possible. <strong>Hôtel Restaurant de la Tour</strong>, 24 quai Général de Gaulle: a historic establishment run by the Mercier family since 1936, on the harbour, dogs accepted with a lead required in common areas.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The exact conditions (precise supplement, weight limit, number of dogs) vary from one establishment to another and can change by season — it's best to confirm directly by phone rather than relying solely on booking platforms' "pets allowed" filters.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Sanary's market, well known throughout the region, is a good morning outing with your dog before the heat of the day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/en/fiche-bandol">Bandol Dog Beach</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-six-fours">Brutal Beach in Six-Fours</a> are both under 15 minutes by car, with a <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-six-fours-les-plages">dog wash in Six-Fours</a> to rinse your dog off after swimming.</p>
